  "description": "Field and boundary probability rasters for 2022: 14,578 COGs at 2.5 m, totaling 5,814,870,475,534 bytes. Each raster has two uint8 bands, field and boundary; probability equals pixel value / 255. Follow the 60 UTM-zone catalogs and their grid-zone catalogs to every item. Each item records its actual model checksum, four source mosaic IDs, projection, bounds and data destination. Field and boundary fractions are descriptive coarsest-overview measurements using uint8 >128 and >64; these are not vector extraction thresholds. Crop coverage preserves the uploaded RAILS index, using AWS 2024/2025 values where shared; the 26XNQ/27XVK r2 fallback lineage is producer-reported; 8 unknown fractions remain null. The STAC GeoParquet mirror contains the same item metadata for bulk queries.",
  "extent": {
    "spatial": {
      "bbox": [
        [
          -179.9342017717571,
          -55.94573440106268,
          179.82032488735825,
          80.16533661756341
        ]
      ]
    },
    "temporal": {
      "interval": [
        [
          "2022-01-01T00:00:00Z",
          "2022-12-31T23:59:59Z"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
